# Runtime defaults
runtime-defaults/Settings.scm
# NO BENCH WiFi OVERLAY HERE, DELIBERATELY -- THIS ONE LEAKED (caught by verify_release 2026-09-16).
# Every other target pulls `optional: runtime-defaults/Settings-local.scm`, and on those the release
# scrub deletes it from the package.  THAT PROTECTION DOES NOT REACH THIS TARGET, because the wasm
# build PACKS data_staged/wasm32_browser into `demo/LambLisp.data` at LINK time: by release time the
# credentials are inside a binary blob, not a file, so deleting the source file cleans nothing.  And
# demo/ ships in EVERY customer package, so one wasm build with an overlay present would have pushed
# the bench SSID and password to ten public repos.  A push cannot be unsent; the remedy would be
# rotating the password.
#
# Nothing is lost: a browser tab has no radio.  Settings-local.scm carries wifi/wifi_ssid/wifi_pass
# and net_test_host, none of which mean anything here.  Do NOT "restore consistency" with the other
# manifests by adding this line back.
# AND NO net-test-ca.pem, FOR THE SAME REASON AND THE SAME MECHANISM.  It is a generated bench
# artifact (written by _w3_run_network), the release scrub deletes it by name on every other
# target, and that scrub cannot reach inside demo/LambLisp.data either -- verified 2026-09-16 that
# a certificate was in fact packed into the blob.  The browser has no TLS peer to verify, so it has
# no use for it.
# B437: the browser gets its OWN pre-heap GC config -- the shared 8K default is MCU-sized and
# merely loading this library on it made the collector fall behind on the demo page.  See the
# file's own header for why a shipped file rather than a compile-time default, and why the
# browser cannot learn its pool size the way a board does.
# NOTE THE PATH: a per-target DIRECTORY, not a rename.  A bare `src -> dest` is NOT supported
# here -- only `optional:` and `dir:` parse the arrow; the plain branch copies the whole line
# as a path and then stages it under its basename.  So the override is a same-named file in a
# wasm/ subdirectory, which stages as Settings-Lamb.scm and keeps the not-optional warning if
# it ever goes missing.
runtime-defaults/wasm/Settings-Lamb.scm

# Test suite
dir: tests/ll_tests -> ll_tests
